caption: The Blood Covenant
setting-component: the-blood-covenant

The Covenant was established by the founders of the current French state or one of its predecessor regimes. The exact founding event, date, original signatories, and legal wording are not yet defined.

The Covenant is national rather than global. Niktul’s protection applies to France and the population covered by the agreement; the exact supernatural definition of France’s borders remains to be decided.

The sacrifice requirement is expected to be on the order of 10,000 people per Blood Moon, though the exact formula is not yet locked. Niktul’s priests can pray to him for guidance on how many sacrifices are required during a given Blood Moon and how many remain outstanding. The quota may ultimately be fixed, population-based, or otherwise derived from the Covenant.

If the quota is fulfilled before dawn, the protection continues through the next lunar month. If it is not fulfilled, the protection ends at dawn and remains absent until France successfully renews the Covenant during a later Blood Moon.
